WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.547
Typed timestamps are more useful for analysis than display strings.

00:00:04.547 --> 00:00:10.327
They sort chronologically, support arithmetic, and retain temporal semantics.

00:00:10.327 --> 00:00:15.747
A formatted string is useful for a person but less flexible for computation.

00:00:15.747 --> 00:00:22.732
That is why formatting generally belongs near the output boundary rather than early in the preparation

00:00:22.732 --> 00:00:30.607
pipeline. Parsing converts text into a typed value; formatting converts a typed value into presentation text.

00:00:30.607 --> 00:00:37.467
Perform analytical work on typed dates and timestamps, then format near the presentation layer.

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:44.282
If parsing can fail, validate the incoming pattern first instead of letting one malformed value stop an entire

00:00:44.282 --> 00:00:45.587
load.
